<title>DENMARK: Denmark's B&amp;O rockets on share buyback.</title>
<headline>Denmark's B&amp;O rockets on share buyback.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGEN 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Danish home electronics maker Bang &amp; Olufsen rose by over nine percent on Wednesday on news that it was buying back Dutch electronics giant Philips' 25 percent stake in the company.</p>
<p>At 0805 GMT the share was up 36 crowns from Tuesday's close, to 416.00.</p>
<p>&quot;There has been great interest from the start and the share could rise a little more,&quot; a dealer said.</p>
<p>Since Tuesday's announcement of the buyback the B&amp;O share has risen a total of 51 crowns. --Steve Weizman, Copenhagen newsroom +45 33 969650</p>
</text>
